    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d89">

                <pb facs="0251" n="119" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg119"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15/391: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-07T19:00:00-03:30"><hi rendition="#italic">October 7,
                                1926—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>53. Your telegram number 23, October 2, 1 p.m. The Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    informed me today that Uruguay will be represented at the next meeting of the
                    Preliminary [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] Disarmament Commission, possibly
                    by Guani.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d89-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d89-f1" n="6" xml:id="d89-f1-content">
                <p>Alberto Guani. On Oct. 9 Mr. Grant-Smith reported Uruguay’s Withdrawal from the
                    Preparatory Commission.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
